<header><p class="enc-kicker">Historical factor</p><h1 class="enc-title">Floods and natural disasters</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Floods and natural disasters, such as river floods, failed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> inundations and earthquakes, could devastate harvests, cities and state revenues. They contributed to the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> floods sparked unrest, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a> during Egyptian famines, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> earthquake of 1755.</p></div>
